{
  "name": "Start",
  "comment": "Where a run goes on is two numbers in its snapshot, each its frame's own: the step's place in its goal and the action's\nplace in its step. Plan saves the run at its step 1; the program moves the stop point to step 3, action 0, signs the\nsnapshot again (it vouches for its own edit), and resumes it: the run goes on at step 3, so step 2 never runs (%b%\nkeeps the value it had when the run was saved) and step 3 does. The resumed run goes on through this goal too, from\nthe step after `call Plan`: the marker sends it to Resumed, which writes what it saw and ends it.",
  "step": [
